            <ArticleTitle>Role of developmental overnutrition in pediatric obesity and type 2 diabetes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>S62-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/nure.12061</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Childhood obesity continues to be a significant public health burden. Empirical evidence has begun to identify intrauterine and postnatal pathways that increase the likelihood of excess adiposity and increased risk of type 2 diabetes among offspring. Reviewed here is the evidence supporting a transgenerational vicious cycle that increases obesity and diabetes in offspring and contributes substantially to the increases in obesity and type 2 diabetes observed over the past several decades. The public health impact of these findings is discussed and future research opportunities are outlined.</AbstractText>
                <CopyrightInformation>© 2013 International Life Sciences Institute.</CopyrightInformation>
            </Abstract>
